N8. the symmetry penalty
   n = 7, u = 9: a 9-arc shaving has |Aut S| <= n!/2^u = 9.84
   n = 8, u = 11: a 11-arc shaving has |Aut S| <= n!/2^u = 19.69
   n = 9, u = 14: a 14-arc shaving has |Aut S| <= n!/2^u = 22.15
PASS Burnside: a 9-shaving with |Aut S| = 2 still has >= 2^21 > T(9) completion orbits, so counting alone does not force rigidity

